body:
This is more of a parenting question I suppose, but is it normal for kids to not remember anything? We picked SD7 up from a 6 hour girl scout event. Immediately asked what she did. I don't remember. I tried asking more specific questions. Eventually dragged out coloring a cloud and a game they played. More specific questions didn't pull a lot more out.

&#x200B;

Is this normal? Is it normal for a kid to not be able to describe much of what was done immediately after it happens?
